    "text": "Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></math> be non-zero complex numbers such that <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow><mo>-</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mo>-</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></math> varies, then the perimeter of the locus of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math>&nbsp;is",
